menu "Filesystem"

config FS_MIGRATE
    bool "Migrate a pre-PEX LittleFS through the SD card"
    default n
    help
      One boot of a board whose LittleFS is still the old 2032 KiB layout.
      Copies every file to the SD card, verifies it, formats the smaller
      filesystem, and restores cfg/ before anything else is read. About 7 KB
      of flash. Off, that file is not linked.

      A filesystem already in the new layout is unchanged either way.
      fs_init() still mounts an old one as found. sys.info and the root of
      /api/fs then say "migration pending: not in this build", and the PEX
      partition stays inside that filesystem so nothing is written over it.
      Turn this on, with CONFIG_SD, for the boot that moves it. A build
      without the card reports the same pending state the migrator always
      did when the card was missing.

endmenu
